# esp-fc CLI script — ESP-FLY (XIAO ESP32-S3) on a 915 MHz ELRS/CRSF receiver
#
# Paste into the CLI tab of Betaflight Configurator 10.10 connected to esp-fc.
# Lines starting with # are comments; if your configurator does not strip
# them, paste the "set" lines one at a time.
#
# Pins are the published esp-fc/XIAO wiring (receiver TX -> GPIO 9, RX -> GPIO 8,
# serial 2). If your RP1 V2 was on other pins, change the two numbers to
# match the wires — see docs/drone-hardware.md section 3. `get pin` shows
# what the board currently has.

set pin_serial_2_rx 9
set pin_serial_2_tx 8
set feature_rx_serial 1

# Failsafe: 0.4 s without packets -> DROP (esp-fc's only stage-2 action).
set failsafe_delay 4
set failsafe_kill_switch 0

# The serial-2 function (Serial Rx) and the receiver provider (CRSF) are set
# in the Ports and Receiver tabs; after doing that, run
#   get serial_2
#   get rx
# and paste the two resulting "set ..." lines here so this file is complete
# for your build.

save
